/**
@page image_operations Image Operations

@section image_common Common Buffer Rules

Resize, crop, and rotate operate on packed pixels with a caller-supplied
positive byte count per pixel. Their source size is `width * height * bpp`.
Conversion uses the FourCC-specific formulas in @ref pixel_formats. All image
buffers are caller-owned and source/destination ranges must not overlap.

@section image_resize Resize

Create one LUT when the same source and destination dimensions are used for
multiple frames. The LUT does not depend on pixel channel order or `bpp`.

@code{.c}
sgl_bilinear_lookup_t *lut;
sgl_result_t result;

lut = sgl_generic_create_bilinear_lut(
    dst_width, dst_height, src_width, src_height);
if (lut == SGL_NULL) {
    result = SGL_ERROR_MEMORY_ALLOCATION;
}
else {
    result = sgl_generic_resize_bilinear(
        pool, lut,
        dst, dst_width, dst_height,
        src, src_width, src_height,
        SGL_BPP32);
    sgl_generic_destroy_bilinear_lut(lut);
}
@endcode

Pass `SGL_NULL` as the LUT for one-shot work. SGL then allocates and destroys a
temporary table. Nearest-neighbor is fastest and preserves exact source pixel
values; bilinear smooths a 2x2 neighborhood; bicubic uses a 4x4 neighborhood.

@section image_crop Crop

Crop coordinates are zero-based and the complete rectangle must fit inside the
source image. The destination has no source stride or padding:

@code{.c}
result = sgl_generic_crop(
    pool,
    src, src_width, src_height,
    dst,
    crop_x, crop_y, crop_width, crop_height,
    SGL_BPP32);
@endcode

Allocate at least `crop_width * crop_height * bpp` destination bytes.

@section image_rotate Rotate

Query dimensions before allocating the caller-owned destination. Positive
angles rotate clockwise. Output pixels outside the source footprint are zero.

@code{.c}
sgl_int32_t dst_width;
sgl_int32_t dst_height;
sgl_int32_t dst_bytes;

result = sgl_get_rotated_dimensions(
    src_width, src_height, angle,
    &dst_width, &dst_height);
dst_bytes = sgl_get_rotated_size(
    src_width, src_height, SGL_BPP32, angle);
if ((result == SGL_SUCCESS) && (dst_bytes > 0)) {
    result = sgl_generic_rotate(
        pool, rotate_lut,
        src, src_width, src_height,
        dst, SGL_BPP32, angle);
}
@endcode

A rotation LUT can be shared by generic and SIMD calls and reused across
frames only when source dimensions and normalized angle are identical.

@section image_convert Convert

Choose the entry point from the source and destination format categories:

| Source | Destination | Generic API | SIMD API |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| RGB | RGB | sgl_generic_rgb2rgb() | sgl_simd_rgb2rgb() |
| RGB | YUV | sgl_generic_rgb2yuv() | sgl_simd_rgb2yuv() |
| YUV | RGB | sgl_generic_yuv2rgb() | sgl_simd_yuv2rgb() |
| YUV | YUV | sgl_generic_yuv2yuv() | sgl_simd_yuv2yuv() |

@code{.c}
result = sgl_generic_rgb2yuv(
    pool,
    rgba, SGL_FOURCC_RGBA,
    nv12, SGL_FOURCC_NV12,
    width, height);
@endcode

Every supported source format can be converted to every supported destination
format in the selected category. When adding alpha to RGB, SGL writes 255;
when removing alpha or converting to YUV, it discards alpha.

@section image_backend Generic and SIMD Backends

Generic functions are always declared. SIMD functions are declared only when
`SGL_CFG_HAS_SIMD` is enabled in the generated `sgl-config.h`. Keep portable
fallback selection at compile time:

@code{.c}
#if defined(SGL_CFG_HAS_SIMD)
result = sgl_simd_crop(pool, src, width, height, dst, x, y, cw, ch, bpp);
#else
result = sgl_generic_crop(pool, src, width, height, dst, x, y, cw, ch, bpp);
#endif
@endcode
*/
